contributingGuides/CONTRIBUTING.md:112:    * Information isn't itself valuable. Not having it isn't inherently a problem; having it isn't itself a solution. Information is only valuable when it enables us to act -- so the problem isn't the lack of information, but the problem is that there is something we aren't doing. Part of the solution might be getting more information -- but the information isn't the whole solution, the solution is that we are doing something with that information that we weren't doing before.
